# Responsibility

Loads configured SQL files, starts each query in the selected Athena database and workgroup, waits for execution state, and returns collected query execution IDs.[^athena-handler]

This function is part of the [Serverless Data Pipeline](../systems/serverless-data-pipeline.md) and is implemented in [serverless-data-pipelines-demo](../repositories/serverless-data-pipelines-demo.md).

# Runtime and Trigger

Terraform deploys the handler as a distinct AWS Lambda through `module.view_lambda` with its own execution role.[^athena-deployment][^athena-lambda-resource] The state machine invokes it to create reporting views after the trusted-zone processing branch.[^pipeline-orchestration]

# Failure Behavior

The handler logs an `AttributeError` when a configured SQL file cannot be used and continues through the query list. The state machine retries Lambda service, timeout, and SSH-related failures.[^athena-handler][^pipeline-orchestration]

# Limitations

The SQL files, view contracts, and query-result semantics were not modeled. Terraform expresses intended deployment and does not prove current Athena or function state.

