# Responsibility

Runs a configured Athena query, processes successful query results through Comprehend, and uploads newline-delimited derived JSON to analytics storage.[^comprehend-handler]

This function is part of the [Serverless Data Pipeline](../systems/serverless-data-pipeline.md) and is implemented in [serverless-data-pipelines-demo](../repositories/serverless-data-pipelines-demo.md).

# Runtime and Trigger

Terraform deploys the handler as a distinct AWS Lambda through `module.comprehend_lambda` with its own execution role.[^comprehend-deployment][^comprehend-lambda-resource] The state machine supplies the SQL file, table, Athena database, analytics bucket, and workgroup.[^pipeline-orchestration]

# Failure Behavior

Comprehend processing occurs only when Athena reports `SUCCEEDED`; otherwise the handler uploads an empty result collection. The state machine retries Lambda service, timeout, and SSH-related failures.[^comprehend-handler][^pipeline-orchestration]

# Limitations

Entity-extraction semantics, SQL contents, and output consumers were not modeled. Terraform expresses intended deployment and does not prove current Athena, Comprehend, storage, or function state.

