# Purpose

The [serverless-data-pipelines-demo repository](../repositories/serverless-data-pipelines-demo.md) implements a modular serverless data-lake pipeline that sources public API data, transforms and catalogs it, and derives analytical outputs.[^sys-readme]

Primary Domain: [Crawler](../domains/crawler.md).

# Architecture

Terraform declares one Step Functions state machine that repeatedly invokes the API sourcing function until pagination completes, then runs catalog crawling and Glue ETL branches before invoking Athena view creation and Comprehend analysis.[^sys-orchestration]

The independently deployed runtime functions are:

* [API Sourcing Function](../components/api-sourcing-function.md)
* [Glue Crawler Initiation Function](../components/glue-crawler-initiation-function.md)
* [Athena Query Execution Function](../components/athena-query-execution-function.md)
* [Comprehend Analysis Function](../components/comprehend-analysis-function.md)

The orchestration, storage, catalogs, crawlers, Glue jobs, Athena resources, and delivery sequence are internal implementation knowledge rather than separate identities in this sparse proposal.

# Limitations

Suggested type `System` is evidence-bound agent intent and requires proposal review.

The Step Functions resource has exact Terraform evidence but no released provider-profile mapping, so it remains orchestration detail rather than an independently typed concept.

The README advertises Python 3.8 while the shared Lambda Terraform module configures `python3.7`; the proposal does not infer which runtime was deployed.[^runtime-readme][^runtime-terraform]

Glue Scala ETL code, Athena SQL and views, schedules, DynamoDB state, IAM/KMS, logging, and every data-zone instantiation were not deeply modeled in this bounded pass.

