# Responsibility

Fetches a configured page from a public API, writes non-empty results to landing storage, and returns `IS_COMPLETE` plus the next `PAGE_NUMBER` for orchestration.[^api-handler]

This function is part of the [Serverless Data Pipeline](../systems/serverless-data-pipeline.md) and is implemented in [serverless-data-pipelines-demo](../repositories/serverless-data-pipelines-demo.md).

# Runtime and Trigger

Terraform deploys the handler as a distinct AWS Lambda through `module.api_lambda`; the shared module points Lambda at `src/main.handler` and configures a Python runtime.[^api-deployment][^api-lambda-resource] The pipeline state machine invokes it as its first task with retry handling.[^pipeline-orchestration]

# Failure Behavior

The handler treats an empty page as normal completion. HTTP, connection, timeout, Lambda service, and SDK failures are retried by the state machine; the handler itself does not define local exception handling in the cited span.[^api-handler][^pipeline-orchestration]

# Limitations

The external API contract and deployed configuration values are not modeled. Terraform expresses intended deployment and does not prove a currently deployed function.

