# Responsibility

Starts the Glue crawler named in its input, waits for crawler state, and returns that state to the caller.[^crawler-handler]

This function is part of the [Serverless Data Pipeline](../systems/serverless-data-pipeline.md) and is implemented in [serverless-data-pipelines-demo](../repositories/serverless-data-pipelines-demo.md).

# Runtime and Trigger

Terraform deploys the handler as a distinct AWS Lambda through `module.crawler_lambda` with a crawler-specific execution role.[^crawler-deployment][^crawler-lambda-resource] The state machine invokes the function for a data-zone crawler and supplies `CRAWLER_NAME`.[^pipeline-orchestration]

# Failure Behavior

An already-running crawler is logged and treated as recoverable before state polling. Other start failures are logged and re-raised; the orchestration retries Lambda service failures and timeouts.[^crawler-handler][^pipeline-orchestration]

# Limitations

One Lambda implementation is reused for multiple data-zone crawlers, but those crawler resources remain embedded infrastructure. Terraform expresses intended deployment and does not prove current crawler or function state.

